;; QUARANTINE. This pattern was MINTED BY A SCRIPT from 3 refusal
;; record(s), under Joe's 2026-09-02 ruling extension: a recurring refusal is
;; recorded as a draft design pattern so the refusals become design knowledge
;; instead of standing red. It is a DRAFT and is quarantined exactly as a
;; @why-posthoc edge is -- counted separately by checks/library_graph_lint.clj,
;; admitted to no authored-authority law, and outside the organised fraction.
;; It carries no @why: a script has no rationale to claim. It earns standing the
;; ordinary way -- a person removes @draft and writes the @why, and that edge
;; then needs its attestation like any other.
;; Regenerated on every sweep. Hand edits to the body will be overwritten;
;; promote it out of draft instead.

! conclusion: A recurring refusal at :prediction-error/v1 is unresolved design work, not a
  standing red. Someone must decide whether the caller or the producer is wrong.

  + context: 3 record(s) of `:source-field-missing` from `:prediction-error/v1`,
    first seen 2026-09-02T13:47:22.082297526Z, last seen 2026-09-02T14:03:09.647517345Z. Harvested
    2026-09-02T15:26:46.632435328Z by holes/labs/wm-contract/harvest_refusals.bb from the WM trace and
    the C130 absence-coercion lint. Statuses: :absent.
    + salience: the producer refuses REPEATEDLY and the refusal has no consumer.
      That is the refuse-and-stop failure mode the ruling of 2026-09-02 names,
      seen from the producer's side.
    + whose problem: the caller's, until someone shows the producer is wrong to
      refuse. The producer stated a reason; nothing downstream acts on it.

  + IF:
    :prediction-error/v1 is asked for a value it can only supply from an input that was
    not observed or was malformed.

  + HOWEVER:
    It refuses with `:source-field-missing`, and has done so 3 time(s); no
    caller repairs the input and no reader turns the refusal into work.

  + THEN:
    EMPTY. No resolution has been written. This half of the pattern is the
    tension recorded before its resolution exists, which is what the ruling
    extension asked for; it is NOT a claim that a resolution is known.

  + BECAUSE:
    A refusal that recurs is a statement about the design, not about the tick.
